laurel 3021: LAUREL GPU MOTION: the GPU governor (2961) waits on an event, not IOSleep: a touch or the first frame after a pause (laurel 3020 laurel_frame_event) wakes it, and it goes to the top usable level at once (950 MHz, DDR 1804 MHz by opp_go's bus vote), not 320 -> 745 -> 950 over two 50 ms ticks; held 300 ms after a touch and 150 ms after the last frame, then by load (lower after 500 ms under the aim). opp_decide takes the level the UI holds (OPP_HOLD_TOP, OPP_TOUCH with gpumotion=0, OPP_NONE) in place of the bool; host test scripts/laurel/test-gpu-opp.sh. The thermal rule (95 C step, 100 C lowest) and the hot refusal count are unchanged. Kill switch gpumotion=0 (2961: a touch holds 745 MHz, read at the tick). Both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/clocks-on-motion.md.

